===Verb===
{{en-verb|pres_ptc2=shenaniganning}} {{term-label|en|originally|US|informal}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[play#Verb|play]] a [[deceitful]] [[confidence trick]] on (someone); to [[swindle#Verb|swindle]], to [[trick#Verb|trick]]; also, to [[carry out]] an [[act#Noun|act]] of [[mischief#Noun|mischief]] on (someone); to [[prank#Verb|prank]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=19 October 1872|title=Notes on the College Press and so forth|journal=The Chronicle|location=Ann Arbor, Mich.|publisher=Students of the {{w|University of Michigan}}|volume=IV|issue=II|page=24|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=QfQfAQAAMAAJ&pg=RA3-PA24|column=2|oclc=29767677|passage=The habit of "'''shenaniganing'''" has become so disgracefully common at Union college that some of the right minded students have passed resolutions condemning the practice in unqualified terms. We are happy to inform the friends of Michigan University that this unmusical word, which, translated means the use of artificial aids, in examinations, is almost wholly unknown here.|footer={{small|A noun use.}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1894|author=Mary J. Jaques|chapter=Sheep Dipping, Breaking in Bronchos, Visit to Texan Squatter|title=Texan Ranch Life; with Three Months through Mexico in a “Prairie Schooner”|location=London|publisher={{w|Horace Cox}},{{nb...|Windsor House, Bream’s Buildings, E.C.}}|pages=114–115|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/texanranchlifewi00jaqurich/page/115/mode/1up|oclc=2161625|passage=I must have looked sceptical regarding the squirrel, as I informed him that I had not much appetite just then; but he assured me he was not "'''shenan-neganning'''" me, and that the dish would prove a delicacy.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|quotee=Amalia Sena Sánchez|chapter=Fiesta|editor=John Pen[daries] La Farge|title=Turn Left at the Sleeping Dog: Scripting the Santa Fe Legend, 1920–1955|location=Albuquerque, N.M.|publisher=w:University of New Mexico Press|page=56|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=R3KZK3_mL7wC&pg=PA56|isbn=978-0-8263-2014-8|passage=Then Jim, the man that was in charge of the booths, {{...}} says, "It's too large. It has to be a regular size." I said, "Look, it can't go back, and we have the place reserved. I've already paid for it." I don't know, he '''shenaniganed''' something.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To play a deceitful confidence trick; also, to carry out an act of mischief.
#* {{quote-hansard|en|date=6 February 1964|speaker=w:Basil Whitener|debate=Civil Rights Act of 1963|report=[[w:Congressional Record|Congressional Record: Proceedings and Debates of the 88th Congress, Second Session]]|house={{w|United States House of Representatives}}|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|United States Government Printing Office]]|volume=110, part 2|page=2260|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=r3q-oKKwD6EC&pg=PA2260|column=3|issn=0363-7239|oclc=13530005|passage=Then after much '''shenaniganing''' around over a period of several weeks {{...}} we came into the committee room after this "night study" which I understand too place, and some of the Members had the bill we are now considering in a mimeographed form and some of us did not have it.}}
#* {{quote-hansard|en|date=9 July 1986|speaker=R. F. H. Maxwell|debate=Debate—General|report=Parliamentary Debates (Hansard): Second Session, Forty-first Parliament|house=[[w:New Zealand House of Representatives|House of Representatives]]|location=Wellington|publisher=V. R. Ward, government printer|volume=472|page=2800|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=SkCDr0i68nsC&pg=PA2800|oclc=191255532|passage=Was it merely a ruse to ensure that the people during that period of 12 months got used to the idea that the workshop would close, and gradually reconciled themselves to it? It does not look as if they have, but I suggest that that is one reason the Government '''shenaniganed''' around with the people of Wanganui.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=Michel Guyon|chapter=From London to Gristlemoth|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=FVQ5EAAAQBAJ&pg=PT51|title=Archibald Finch and the Lost Witches|location=Kansas City, Mo.|publisher=w:Andrews McMeel Publishing|isbn=978-1-5248-6772-0|passage=I'm just '''shenaniganning''' with you. Keep your hair in your face and your mouth shut and it will be fine.}}

